  "name": "colocated_mode_swap_loop_pauli_zz",
  "kind": "synth",
  "contract": "exact",
  "idea": "exp(-i theta Z_j Z_k) (and XX/YY by single-qubit basis change) for neighbouring qubits via a Heisenberg-Weyl closed phase-space loop using no ancilla qumode: the bus state is shuttled between the two co-located qumodes m_j, m_k (one qumode per qubit site) by full beam-splitter swaps S = BS(pi,0), with S^4 = I. The sequence CD_j(alpha) S CD_k(beta) S CD_j(alpha) S CD_k(beta) S conjugates each CD_k displacement into mode m_j's frame (S^+ a S = -i b, S^2 a S^{+2} = -a, S^3 a S^{+3} = i b), closing a rectangle D_a(-iB) D_a(-A) D_a(iB) D_a(A) whose commutator phase D(u)D(v)D(-u)D(-v) = exp(u v* - u* v) gives exp(2i alpha beta Z_j Z_k) exactly, with mode m_k returned untouched (S^4 = I) and mode m_j returned to vacuum. Choosing alpha = sqrt(|theta|/2), beta = -sign(theta) * alpha gives exactly exp(-i theta Z_j Z_k). Every two-mode gate is either co-located (CD on q_j-m_j, q_k-m_k) or a BS on the neighbouring mode pair (m_j,m_k), so the router adds no SWAPs when m_j, m_k are grid neighbours.",
  "term_kinds": [
   "pauli"
  ],
  "stage": "logical"
 },
